Hello and welcome to Speaking of Psychology, a podcast produced by the American Psychological Association. I am your host, Audrey Hamilton. In this episode, I talk with a psychologist about having those difficult but important end-of-life discussions with your loved ones. Psychology has a lot to add in terms of what we know about how people make decisions, manage their emotions, and handle relationships, all things that can affect how we approach these discussions. These are difficult things for people to bring up. They're not sure how to do it, but we know it's important for them to plan and to think ahead. So we want to give people a sense of confidence and competence that they know how to bring up these topics. Yes, I know. Talking about death sounds depressing.
你好，欢迎收听《心理学说话》，这是一档由美国心理学会制作的播客。我是主持人奥黛丽·汉密尔顿。在本期节目中，我和一位心理学家探讨了如何与挚爱进行那些困难但却重要的临终讨论。心理学在帮助我们理解人们如何做决策、管理情绪以及处理人际关系方面有很多可以贡献的内容，所有这些都会影响我们如何看待这些讨论。对人们来说，提起这些事情很困难。他们不确定该怎么做，但我们知道，对他们来说提前规划和思考是很重要的。因此，我们希望赋予人们一种自信和能力，让他们知道如何提起这些话题。是的，我知道。谈论死亡听起来很压抑。

